target/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/

# The working copy `contract-mutations.py` holds while it breaks a library rule on purpose,
# runs the suite, and puts the original back. It exists for seconds at a time -- but while it
# does, the real file is DELIBERATELY BROKEN and this one holds the good bytes. Committing in
# that window would take both: a mutated library, and a stray copy explaining nothing.
# Seen on 2026-09-25, when two runs overlapped and `git status` showed exactly that pair.
*.mutating
